### 5. User Interface & Operational Readiness
**PS Requirement:** Transform current decentralized and manual block planning into a data-driven, coordinated process.

**What you built:**
- 11 full React pages: Dashboard, Request Inbox, AI Planner, Block Plans, Train Dispatch, Safety & Conflicts, Maintenance Board, Asset Health, What-If Simulator, Analytics, Login
- **AI Planner Console** with NLP interface (Hindi/English) powered by Qwen-2.5 via Ollama
- **What-If Simulator** with 5 perturbation types: remove train, delay train, add special train, change task severity, add emergency task
- Role-based access control (Controller vs Department users)
- Full CRUD lifecycle: Request → Review → Accept → AI Plan → Approve → Publish → Block Register
- Safety report transparency on every block plan (checks passed/failed, rejection reasons)

**Strengths:**
- The UI is production-quality. Dark theme, proper icons, responsive layout
- End-to-end workflow from departmental request to approved block plan is fully functional
- The What-If simulator is a genuine differentiator — most SIH teams won't have this
- NLP interface with Hindi support shows awareness of real user needs

**Weaknesses:**
- No mobile responsiveness (railway controllers often use tablets)
- No real-time notifications via WebSocket (polling-based)
- Dashboard analytics are somewhat basic (no trend analysis or comparative views)

> **Score: 8.5 / 10**

